{"id": "3c6ed5b0-d32a-487c-83fb-209a4c0a7387", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is asking about AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks for SSH troubleshooting—I'm recalling AWSSupport-TroubleshootSSH, which uses the EC2Rescue tool to diagnose and fix sshd configuration issues on Linux instances, and there's also AWSSupport-ExecuteEC2Rescue for related tasks.

For connection timeouts specifically, the cause is usually network-related (security groups, NACLs, route tables, missing public IP), so I'm weighing whether the right runbook is a connectivity troubleshooter rather than TroubleshootSSH itself. Since I don't have verify_aws_claim available directly and this is a factual AWS product detail I'm not fully certain of, I think the safer path is delegating verification to a subagent rather than stating specifics I can't confirm.

